Description: FreeBSD ports patch of the curl configure: accept -D in CFLAGS and -l in LDFLAGS, keep the -O flags of CFLAGS (PR 150854, 177401, 180944); conncache: an idle HTTP/1.1 connection with input pending is not reused (the stray bytes came back as the response to the next request, and every later one was shifted)
Origin: freebsd-ports ftp/curl/files/patch-configure @ f3611d920828, unchanged; upstream https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/ef6b17cf12d4af4dfb2af4f9bc35861772be71c7 (lib/conncache.c, after 8.23.0; as Gentoo net-misc/curl 8.23.0-r1 carries it)

